   },
   {
      "type":"paragraph",
      "index":8,
      "text":[
         "Ashen never triggered a cut scene. He never offered lore.",
         "When asked questions like “How do you know that?” or “Why are you",
         "still here?”— he only shrugged, smiled, scoffed, waved off, or let",
         "out a tired groan as if frustrated by being asked such questions too many",
         "times. He would rarely say something short and vague like “I’m on watch”",
         "while gesturing to nothing in particular."
      ]
   },
   {
      "type":"paragraph",
      "index":9,
      "text":[
         "He could speak to places sometimes. An example is when he acknowledges the",
         "absence of long forgotten buildings like the town watchtower.",
         "“Still holding,” he murmured to the old bridge once.",
         "He watched the grass grow where a battlefield had been.",
         "“Good,” he said softly. “They finally let you rest.”"
      ]
   },
   {
      "type":"paragraph",
      "index":10,
      "text":[
         "Ashen never moves away from his spot even in the rain or winter. But",
         "somehow he is always looking well-protected from the present weather,",
         "maybe with a long coat or any other proper clothing."
      ]
   },
   {
      "type":"paragraph",
      "index":11,
      "text":[
         "Some players began stopping by on purpose. Not to gain anything; just to",
         "stand near him. He made the world feel deeper or older like things had",
         "happened here that mattered."
      ]
   },
   {
      "type":"paragraph",
      "index":12,
      "text":[
         "Ashen remained even when names changed, settings evolved, and stories",
         "shifted."
      ]
   },
